Black coffee has essentially no carbs. A cup of brewed coffee has less than a gram, and so does a shot of espresso. The carbs come from what goes in it: sugar, syrups, sweetened creamers and milk.

That's a big deal for blood sugar. A coffee-shop latte with a couple pumps of syrup can easily have more sugar than a can of soda, and a few spoonfuls of a sweetened creamer every morning adds up fast. But you don't have to give up good coffee, or even milky coffee, to keep it low-carb.

This is the overview. Each part has its own guide.

## 1. Learning to drink coffee black

The easiest low-carb coffee is black coffee, and it's a lot easier to enjoy when the coffee is good. Some beans and roasts taste sweet all on their own, and a few brewing changes make a big difference too.

**Read more:** [Learning to Drink Coffee Black](/coffee/guides/learning-to-drink-coffee-black/).

## 2. Unsweetened milks and creamers

If you like milk in your coffee, the kind you pick matters. Unsweetened soy, coconut and pea milks have very few carbs, and cream has fewer than milk. Oat milk has more than most people expect, even when it says "no added sugar."

**Read more:** [Unsweetened Milks and Creamers](/coffee/guides/unsweetened-milks-and-creamers/), with a chart of carbs per splash and per latte.

## 3. Frothing milk at home

A latte or cappuccino at home doesn't need an espresso machine or any syrup. A cheap frother and some warm milk get you most of the way there, and you get to choose exactly what goes in it.

**Read more:** [Frothing Milk at Home](/coffee/guides/frothing-milk-at-home/).

## The short version

- **Start with good beans.** Good coffee needs less help. [Understanding Coffee Beans](/coffee/guides/understanding-coffee-beans/) is a good place to find coffee you'll like.
- **Brew it well.** A lot of "I need sugar" is really bitter, over-extracted coffee. [Brewing Basics](/coffee/guides/brewing-basics/) covers the fixes.
- **Pick an unsweetened milk** and watch out for flavored creamers.
- **If you want it sweet,** a zero-carb sweetener works. I use [monk fruit](/ingrts/monk-fruit-sweetener/) drops in coffee.
